--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components distributed with Vectispire
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The application jar and the container image built from `Dockerfile` bundle the
following components. Their own licenses apply to them, not Vectispire's.

Apache License 2.0
  org.springframework.boot:*                Spring Boot 4.1
  org.springframework:*                     Spring Framework
  org.hibernate.orm:*                       Hibernate ORM
  com.fasterxml.jackson.core:*              Jackson
  org.apache.pdfbox:pdfbox                  PDFBox
  org.apache.httpcomponents.client5:*       Apache HttpClient 5
  org.flywaydb:*                            Flyway
  com.github.docker-java:*                  docker-java

BSD 3-Clause / Eclipse Distribution License 1.0
  org.eclipse.jgit:*                        JGit and its Apache SSH transport
  org.postgresql:postgresql                 PostgreSQL JDBC driver (BSD-2-Clause)

MIT
  org.bouncycastle:bcprov-jdk18on           Bouncy Castle provider
  org.bouncycastle:bcpkix-jdk18on           Bouncy Castle PKIX

GPL-2.0 WITH Universal-FOSS-Exception-1.0
  com.mysql:mysql-connector-j               MySQL Connector/J

  Vectispire ships two JDBC drivers, and one of them is copyleft. Both are
  `runtimeOnly` in the build: no compiled Vectispire class links against a driver,
  and the connection is obtained through the JDBC API. MySQL Connector/J is
  distributed under the GPL with Oracle's Universal FOSS Exception, whose list of
  permitted licenses includes Apache-2.0 — which is what makes shipping it inside
  an Apache-2.0 image lawful. Replacing that license with a copyleft-incompatible
  one, or linking a driver at compile time, breaks that and is the reason this
  paragraph exists rather than a bare list.

